00:00:48.048 --> 00:00:48.506
- Nate,

00:00:48.923 --> 00:00:49.924
you're 5'9", 

00:00:49.924 --> 00:00:52.635
and the things that you've been able to accomplish 
throughout the course of your career, 

00:00:52.635 --> 00:00:53.803
a lot of people would say

00:00:53.803 --> 00:00:56.347
it's virtually impossible to be able to do something like that. 

00:00:56.347 --> 00:00:58.475
- I just wanted to prove, you know,
so many people wrong

00:00:58.475 --> 00:01:00.268
and all the doubters. Like, look,

00:01:00.268 --> 00:01:02.562
even though I'm 5'9",
I don't see myself as being short.

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:04.064
I just like to have fun. And

00:01:04.064 --> 00:01:05.774
I go out there and play with my heart on my sleeve,

00:01:05.774 --> 00:01:06.900
and I show what I got,

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.693
and it's been working over the years.

00:01:08.693 --> 00:01:10.236
- When it's Nate against the world, man,

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:10.945
how does that feel?

00:01:10.945 --> 00:01:12.489
How do you thrive in those moments?

00:01:12.489 --> 00:01:13.823
- You know, you rise to the occasion. 

00:01:13.823 --> 00:01:17.327
My dad always told me, “Man, when the lights come on, 
you gotta be ready to perform.”

00:01:17.327 --> 00:01:21.539
When it's time, and it's some nights you may wake up, play against LeBron or

00:01:21.539 --> 00:01:24.292
play against Kobe and different players,

00:01:24.292 --> 00:01:25.085
you just gotta be ready. 

00:01:25.085 --> 00:01:27.128
When you get the opportunity, you gotta make the best of it.

00:01:27.128 --> 00:01:28.213
And I tried to do that.

00:01:29.672 --> 00:01:33.885
- Talk to me, man. What was the thing that comes to mind when you think about 
the challenges you faced in New York with Mike D'Antoni?

00:01:33.885 --> 00:01:34.969
- It was tough, man.

00:01:34.969 --> 00:01:35.804
People don't know

00:01:35.804 --> 00:01:39.682
the shit I used to go through. I used to try to, you know, have 
meetings with him and try to figure out why I wasn't playing.

00:01:39.682 --> 00:01:41.226
And he just didn't wanna speak to me.

00:01:41.226 --> 00:01:42.894
Ignored me sometimes, and

00:01:42.894 --> 00:01:43.853
he would—
- He didn't explain at all?

00:01:43.853 --> 00:01:45.230
- Didn't even explain it to me.

00:01:45.230 --> 00:01:46.606
- How many games did you go without playing?

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:47.273
- 14, bro.

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:48.024
- 14 straight games.

00:01:48.024 --> 00:01:49.234
- 14 straight games, bro. And then like,

00:01:49.234 --> 00:01:51.986
when I'm at The Garden, people are screaming, "We want Nate." 
They screamed—like, the whole crowd.

00:01:51.986 --> 00:01:54.072
Like, imagine 20,000 people screaming,

00:01:54.072 --> 00:01:55.281
"Put in Nate. We want Nate." 

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:56.991
So, I remember one time, during New Year’s,

00:01:56.991 --> 00:01:58.660
I called my mom. I was like, "Mom,

00:01:58.660 --> 00:01:59.744
come chill in Atlanta with me.

00:01:59.744 --> 00:02:01.538
You know, I need a familiar face, pick-me-up,

00:02:01.538 --> 00:02:02.914
cuz I ain't been playing.” I was like,

00:02:02.914 --> 00:02:05.416
"It'd be good to have you at the game, just to be there, just so I know you’re there.”

00:02:05.416 --> 00:02:06.459
The game goes on.

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:07.418
First quarter,

00:02:07.418 --> 00:02:09.462
Coach calls my name, and I didn't move.

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:12.257
I just stood there like, you know, we're in the huddle. He's like, "Nate."

00:02:12.257 --> 00:02:14.092
And I was like, "Shit, I know he ain't talkin’ to me."

00:02:14.092 --> 00:02:16.803
And then my team was like, "Nate, he callin’ you, fool. Go!” I was like, “Oh, shit.

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:17.762
I took my jersey off.

00:02:17.762 --> 00:02:19.430
- In my head, I was thinking about The Waterboy.

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:20.390
I was like, “Man.”

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:22.559
You know, like Waterboy, when they were like, "Water sucks!"

00:02:22.559 --> 00:02:25.019
You know what I'm saying? He’s picturing the coach’s face.

00:02:25.019 --> 00:02:28.481
I was picturing everybody’s face on the team was D'Antoni.

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:29.315
- [Laughing]

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:31.818
- I was like, "I'm out here.

00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:32.861
I'm out here. It's time."

00:02:32.861 --> 00:02:33.987
So, I went in the game,

00:02:33.987 --> 00:02:35.572
and I made like three, four in a row.

00:02:35.572 --> 00:02:40.160
I made a pull-up three, and then after the three that came, 
I had a fadeaway jumper, and I was like, "Oh, yeah, it's on.

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:40.952
It's on and crackin’.”

00:02:40.952 --> 00:02:42.579
And then we end up going to overtime.

00:02:42.579 --> 00:02:45.165
Come to look at the stats, we win the game,

00:02:45.165 --> 00:02:46.124
41 points. 

00:02:46.124 --> 00:02:47.125
- 41 points?

00:02:47.125 --> 00:02:49.502
- Yep. Six, seven rebounds. Six, seven assists.

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:50.461
Couple steals.

00:02:50.461 --> 00:02:51.963
Had a hell of a game, man.

00:02:51.963 --> 00:02:55.175
And I ain't gonna lie, I think I cried after that game cuz it was—I was just so happy.

00:02:55.175 --> 00:02:55.550
- Is this your shot?

00:02:55.550 --> 00:02:56.551
- Yup.

00:02:56.551 --> 00:02:57.552
We'll roll with this.

00:02:59.762 --> 00:03:02.432
- Nate, three-time Slam Dunk Contest champion.

00:03:02.432 --> 00:03:03.766
Ain't nobody else done that.

00:03:03.766 --> 00:03:04.726
First person to ever do it.

00:03:04.726 --> 00:03:06.060
Which one's your favorite, man?

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:07.687
- Spud, bringing out Spud.

00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:10.565
I got a call from Jamal Crawford one day. He was calling me.

00:03:10.565 --> 00:03:14.235
He was like, "Bro!" I was like, "Bro, wassup, Mal?” I said, “You sound excited.” 

00:03:14.235 --> 00:03:16.529
He was like, "Bro, I am. I got a perfect idea for you for the dunk contest." 

00:03:16.529 --> 00:03:18.156
I was like, "Bro, shoot it! Wassup?"

00:03:18.156 --> 00:03:21.075
He was like, "Bro, you should bring out Spud Webb and jump over him."

00:03:21.075 --> 00:03:22.744
And I was like, "Spud Webb?” Like—

00:03:22.744 --> 00:03:25.330
I said, "But that’d be too easy to just jump over Spud Webb." They were like,

00:03:25.330 --> 00:03:27.457
“It's not about being easy. It's about the scene.”

00:03:27.457 --> 00:03:28.875
- Shoutout Jamal Crawford for the idea.

00:03:28.875 --> 00:03:30.376
- Yeah, shoutout to Mal. Shoutout to Spud.

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:33.755
We kinda changed the way the dunk contest was.

00:03:33.755 --> 00:03:35.673
Cuz before that, it was just, you know,

00:03:35.673 --> 00:03:38.343
start bringing out guys like that. Then, you know, jumping over Dwight,

00:03:38.343 --> 00:03:39.802
over Superman. That was tough.

00:03:39.802 --> 00:03:40.762
That was, that was difficult.

00:03:40.762 --> 00:03:41.304
- [Laughing]

00:03:41.304 --> 00:03:42.388
- And then that was born, what,

00:03:42.388 --> 00:03:43.181
KryptoNate, right?

00:03:43.181 --> 00:03:44.557
- Yup. And KryptoNate was born.

00:03:44.891 --> 00:03:45.516
- Hell yeah

00:03:45.850 --> 00:03:47.101
- That’s what happened.
- How'd those shoes come about, man? 

00:03:47.101 --> 00:03:48.811
That's what I need answers about more, man.

00:03:48.811 --> 00:03:50.813
- I told Nike—I’m like, “Man, I got a perfect dunk

00:03:50.813 --> 00:03:53.858
I got a dunk that I wanna do in the dunk contest." And I was talking to them,

00:03:53.858 --> 00:03:56.736
and I was like, "But I need some shoes."

00:03:56.736 --> 00:03:59.030
And then they came up with

00:03:59.030 --> 00:04:02.867
the Kryptonite that was the Foamposite. I was like, 
"Oooh, with the green.” I was like, “Yo!”

00:04:02.867 --> 00:04:06.287
And I gave ‘em the whole KryptoNate thing, and they were like, "Yeah, 
we gonna, we gonna run with this."

00:04:06.287 --> 00:04:09.082
They gave me a sleeve and a whole green jersey for the Knicks.

00:04:09.082 --> 00:04:10.416
- The green
- But believe it or not, that day,

00:04:10.416 --> 00:04:12.961
when they made me the shoes, somebody stole ‘em out my hotel.

00:04:12.961 --> 00:04:15.505
- Like, how—OK, so, you had the shoes on you.

00:04:15.505 --> 00:04:17.131
- I went to go do all my media stuff.

00:04:17.131 --> 00:04:18.883
I did all my media stuff, and I come back to my room,

00:04:18.883 --> 00:04:19.592
and they were gone.

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:20.885
Somebody put ‘em on eBay.

00:04:20.885 --> 00:04:23.304
Cuz they had never been seen before. Nobody even seen ‘em.

00:04:23.304 --> 00:04:25.265
So when they seen ‘em on eBay, they were like, "Yo!"

00:04:25.265 --> 00:04:28.226
